## Help reference window (macOS)

Open **Help → Keyboard Shortcuts** (`⌘/`) for the in-app shortcut reference window—a curated table maintained alongside the command catalog. The command palette also lists **Settings: Keyboard Shortcuts (Advanced)** to jump there quickly.

Custom rebinding, when available, is configured in that reference UI—not duplicated here.

## Vim-style navigation (macOS)

When card focus is active (`⌃L`), use single-key navigation in lists and triage grids:

### List mode (Focused layout)

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `j` | Move down |
| `k` | Move up |
| `⇧J` / `⇧K` | Extend batch selection |
| `Space` | Toggle selection / open focused item |
| `v` | Enter selection mode |

### Grid mode (Triage card grid)

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `h` | Move left |
| `j` | Move down |
| `k` | Move up |
| `l` | Move right |
| `Space` | Focus current card in view (does not open reader) |

Arrow keys work in both surfaces. **Cycle focus** between sidebar and cards with `⌃Tab`. Built-in vim bindings are always available when card focus is active—they are not a separate settings toggle.

## Naming corrections

Older guides may say **“Move to folder”** — the catalog command is **Move…** (`⌘⇧M`).  
**Archive** has no default shortcut; use the command or actions palette.

